# Aesthetic Standards - Phase 1 Implementation

**Status**: Active - Enforces Phase 1 aesthetic improvements
**Reference**: `docs/AESTHETIC_IMPROVEMENTS_IMPLEMENTATION.md`

## Color Palette: Service Design Leader

### MANDATORY: Use Theme Tokens Only

❌ **NEVER use hardcoded colors**:

```css
/* FORBIDDEN */
color: #ffffff;
background: #0f2851;
border-color: #d97706;
```

✅ **ALWAYS use theme tokens**:

```css
/* CORRECT */
color: var(--color-primary-contrast);
background: var(--color-primary-main);
border-color: var(--color-secondary-main);
```

### Color Usage Guidelines

**Primary (Deep Navy #0F2851)**: 60% of usage

- Headings and titles
- Navigation background
- Primary buttons and CTAs
- Strong emphasis text

**Secondary (Warm Rust #D97706)**: 30% of usage

- Call-to-action buttons
- Links and interactive elements
- Warm accents and highlights
- Success state indicators

**Accent (Sage Green #059669)**: 10% of usage

- Success states
- Secondary CTAs
- Growth/transformation highlights
- Service-related iconography

### Token Reference

See: `src/styles/theme/colors.ts`

**Available tokens**:

- `var(--color-primary-main)`, `var(--color-primary-light)`, `var(--color-primary-dark)`
- `var(--color-secondary-main)`, `var(--color-secondary-light)`, `var(--color-secondary-dark)`
- `var(--color-accent-main)`, `var(--color-accent-light)`, `var(--color-accent-dark)`
- `var(--color-text-primary)`, `var(--color-text-secondary)`, `var(--color-text-tertiary)`
- `var(--color-background-primary)`, `var(--color-background-secondary)`

**Full documentation**: `docs/COLOR_PALETTE_OPTIONS.md`

## Animation System

### MANDATORY: Use Unified Animation System

❌ **NEVER create duplicate keyframes**:

```css
/* FORBIDDEN - duplicates existing animation */
@keyframes fadeInUp {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(20px);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
}
```

✅ **ALWAYS use existing animations**:

```html
<!-- Use utility classes -->
<div class="animate-fade-in-up">Content</div>

<!-- Or reference keyframes -->
<style>
  .my-component {
    animation: fadeInUp 600ms cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.2, 1) forwards;
  }
</style>
```

### Available Animations

**Entrance animations**:

- `.animate-fade-in-up` - Fade in from below (most common)
- `.animate-fade-in` - Simple opacity fade
- `.animate-scale-in` - Scale up while fading
- `.animate-slide-in-right` - Slide from left
- `.animate-slide-in-left` - Slide from right

**Interaction animations**:

- `.hover-lift` - Lift effect for cards/buttons
- `.hover-scale` - Scale effect for images
- `.hover-glow` - Glow effect for interactive elements

**Loading states**:

- `.loading-pulse` - Pulse animation
- `.loading-spin` - Spin animation
- `.skeleton` - Skeleton loading effect

**Scroll-triggered**:

```html
<div data-fade>Fades in when scrolled into view</div>
```

### Animation System Files

- **TypeScript**: `src/styles/theme/animations.ts`
- **CSS Utilities**: `src/styles/animations.css`
- **Documentation**: `docs/AESTHETIC_IMPROVEMENTS_IMPLEMENTATION.md#4-unified-animation-system`

### Accessibility REQUIREMENT

✅ **ALWAYS respect reduced motion**:

```css
/* This is automatic in animations.css, but if adding custom animations: */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .my-animation {
    animation: none;
  }
}
```

## Inline Styles

### FORBIDDEN: No Inline Styles

❌ **NEVER use style attribute**:

```astro
<!-- FORBIDDEN -->
<Heading style="color: var(--color-text-primary);">Title</Heading>
<div style="padding: 20px;">Content</div>
```

✅ **ALWAYS use CSS classes**:

```astro
<!-- CORRECT -->
<Heading class="hero-headline">Title</Heading>
<div class="p-5">Content</div>
```

### Process for Removing Inline Styles

1. Identify the inline style
2. Create appropriate CSS class in component stylesheet
3. Replace style attribute with class
4. Import component stylesheet

**Example**: See `src/components/sections/home/Hero.astro` and `src/styles/components/hero.css`

## Component Styling Pattern

### Required Structure

1. **Component file** (`.astro`, `.tsx`)
   - Import component stylesheet
   - Use only classes, no inline styles
   - Use theme tokens via classes

2. **Component stylesheet** (`src/styles/components/[name].css`)
   - All component-specific styles
   - Use theme tokens via `var(--color-*)`
   - Include dark mode variants

3. **TypeScript types** (if needed)
   - Define prop interfaces
   - Export types for reuse

### Example: Proper Component Structure

```astro
---
// src/components/ui/MyComponent.astro
import '@/styles/components/my-component.css';

interface Props {
  title: string;
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary';
}

const { title, variant = 'primary' } = Astro.props;
---

<div class={`my-component my-component--${variant}`}>
  <h2 class="my-component__title">{title}</h2>
</div>
```

```css
/* src/styles/components/my-component.css */
@reference "tailwindcss";

.my-component {
  @apply rounded-lg p-6;
  background-color: var(--color-background-secondary);
}

.my-component__title {
  @apply text-2xl font-bold;
  color: var(--color-text-primary);
}

.my-component--primary {
  border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary-main);
}

.my-component--secondary {
  border-left: 4px solid var(--color-secondary-main);
}

/* Dark mode */
:root[data-theme='dark'] .my-component {
  background-color: var(--color-background-tertiary);
}
```

## Pre-Commit Checklist

Before committing ANY style-related changes:

- [ ] No hardcoded colors (search for `#` in CSS)
- [ ] No inline `style` attributes in components
- [ ] Animation uses unified system (no duplicate keyframes)
- [ ] Component has dedicated stylesheet in `src/styles/components/`
- [ ] Dark mode styles included (`:root[data-theme="dark"]`)
- [ ] Accessibility considered (contrast, reduced motion)
- [ ] Theme tokens used consistently

## Linting Violations

**Auto-fix where possible**:

```bash
# Check for hardcoded colors
grep -r "#[0-9A-F]\{6\}" src/styles/components/ --exclude-dir=node_modules

# Check for inline styles
grep -r "style=" src/components/ --exclude-dir=node_modules
```

